###############################################################################
#  These files are BYTE-VERBATIM extractions from Merlin-proDos2.23.dsk, made by
#  an implementation other than Casso's. They are the oracle the DOS 3.3 reader
#  is measured against, so any transformation destroys what they are for.
#
#  THEY LOOK LIKE TEXT AND ARE NOT. A Merlin source stored as DOS 3.3 type B
#  carries a 4-byte load/length header and ends its lines with a bare CR, so the
#  repository root's `* text=auto` would rewrite the endings and inflate every
#  file by one byte per line -- leaving a fixture that still reads perfectly as
#  Merlin source while no longer being the bytes on the disk. That is the worst
#  possible failure for an oracle: wrong, and authoritative-looking.
#
#  THIS IS WHY THEY ARE NOT UNDER Fixtures/Merlin. That directory holds the same
#  four names, stored deliberately as Windows text because they feed
#  `CassoCli merlin` and a corpus test asserts the CRLF is there. Two different
#  artifacts, two different requirements; sharing a path made the merge pick one
#  and silently break the other.
###############################################################################
* binary
